    {
      "path": "/source/inventory/1/description",
      "operation": "replace",
      "before": "Solid x/y axes meet at source label O. Positive directions have arrowheads to the right and up; negative ends meet the left/bottom frame without arrowheads. Visible axis labels are x, y, O and one positive 1 on each axis at the first grid interval. No other numeric axis labels or independent short tick marks are visible. Arrow tips remain inside the grid boundary in the draft.",
      "after": "Visible ink: solid coordinate axes, positive right/up arrowheads, x, y, O text and two positive unit 1 labels. O has no source point glyph; the mapped O is text, not the hidden origin anchor. The hidden origin is an unchanged construction addition retained for circle and displacement assertions. y and y-unit text have fixed left clearance as the bounded old-FAIL repair; axis geometry, labels and units are unchanged."
    },
    {
      "path": "/source/inventory/1/objects/2",
