      "before": "fig-16-origin",
      "after": "fig-16-origin-text"
    },
    {
      "path": "/source/inventory/2/description",
      "operation": "replace",
      "before": "One solid unfilled closed circle centered on O, with radius ten grid units, fully inside the frame. Extrema are (-10,0), (10,0), (0,10), (0,-10); no labels or independent point dots occur at these intercepts. Existing equation x^2+y^2=100 appears near the upper-right arc. There is no dashed arc, open endpoint, direction arrow, radius dimension or extra sampling guide. Zero-size extrema anchors are construction additions only. O and all four extrema have mapped internal displacement and radius relationships.",
      "after": "Visible ink: one solid unfilled closed circle centered at the axes crossing and the existing upper-right x^2+y^2=100 equation. Source has no independent point dots at O or the four circle-axis extrema. Radius 10 and exact extrema are equation-bound regularization. Hidden origin/extrema are construction additions only, not source-visible point objects, and need no source pointRelationships group. All unchanged radius/displacement assertions remain mapped and executable."
    },
