    {
      "path": "/source/inventory/3/description",
      "operation": "replace",
      "before": "One solid descending straight line, printed x+y=-2, clipped at the top frame near x=-16,y=14 and bottom frame near x=11,y=-13. Both terminals are boundary cuts, not arrowheads, endpoint dots or permission to extend beyond the panel. The printed equation and counted frame determine the regularized terminals exactly. Existing labelled intersections A(-8,6) at upper-left and B(6,-8) at lower-right lie on both the line and circle. No unprinted line-intercept coordinate labels or projection guides are added. Zero-size terminal anchors preserve the source cuts without drawing markers. Both labelled points and both terminals have mapped internal line relationships; A and B also have coordinate relations to mapped O and radius-10 incidence.",
      "after": "Visible ink: one solid descending finite line with x+y=-2 text, two labelled intersections A(-8,6) upper-left and B(6,-8) lower-right. Source has no independent dots at its top/bottom frame cuts. Exact (-16,14) and (11,-13) hidden terminals are unchanged equation/frame-bound construction additions, not mapped source-visible points. A/B point emphasis and upright equation typography remain existing modern additions. A and B are the only mapped point objects; unchanged A-to-B displacement covers both wholly within this group. All old terminal/incidence/origin relationships remain executable without claiming those anchors are visible."
    },
